WEBVTT

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.460
<i>When I was little, I liked 
to peek at the customers,</i>

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:16.070
<i>seeing them enjoy their time.</i>

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.470
<i>My grandfather always smiled pleasantly,</i>

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.600
<i>and Rokuhoudou was always warm.</i>

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.010
You're watching again?

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.260
Kyousui...

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.270
Do you really love this place that much?

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.450
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:21.370
<b>"It Begins with Omurice"</b>

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.330
Gure, could you give me a hand?

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:32.840
Coming.

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.250
Are we moving that?

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:36.560
Yeah.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.080
I thought I'd put it in the sun.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:38.720
There.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.440
Let's give you plenty of sunlight.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:51.570
H-How about we put this one in the sun, too?

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.040
All right, let's move all of them, then.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.970
All of them?!

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:55.610
All.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.040
This is...

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:07.700
Thanks for working so 
hard all day, everyone.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.660
Let's take a break.

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:11.860
Tea, huh? Nice.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:13.170
I'm exhausted.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.420
I'll go switch out Kinako's water, too.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.730
Kinako, would you like some water?

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.550
I'll leave it here, then.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:34.230
Long day for you, too, huh?

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.730
It feels so nice here.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.170
<b>You just need to drink!</b>

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:58.970
Good work, everyone.

00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:00.620
Good work.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.760
Are you not leaving yet, Kyousui-kun?

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.560
I'm almost done. I'm going to finish it off.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.790
Don't work too hard.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:08.760
Okay.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.560
Today's omurice turned out pretty good.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.660
It's a little on the sour side, though.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.560
Now, then...

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.320
Let's start.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:13.000
<b>Comparisons in Coffee Flavors    The Elegant World of Coffee
How to Make Delicious Coffee    Coffee Basics 
World Coffee Directory    Coffee Dictionary</b>

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.210
"Let it settle at medium heat."

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.600
It's pretty bitter.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:33.470
Maybe I should use hotter water.

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:39.770
Sheesh.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.800
I'm nowhere near Grandpa's coffee yet.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:57.400
<i>I wonder what my grandfather felt 
as he stood here every day.</i>

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.850
<i>I have a dream.</i>

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:05.260
<i>I want to inherit Rokuhoudou one day.</i>

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:10.260
<i>That dream is within reach for me now.</i>

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:12.950
<i>But...</i>

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:16.640
Oh, dear.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:19.400
I've been using it for a long time now.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.780
I wanted some new tableware, anyway.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.330
It's a good time.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.900
I think I'll go back <i>there</i> again.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.200
<b>Craft Market</b>

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.710
There're all kinds of things here.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:48.580
<i>This would be great to have at Rokuhoudou.</i>

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.590
<i>It would stand out on the 
amber-colored tables.</i>

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:54.220
<i>It sits well in the hand, too.</i>

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.440
Do you like it?

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:58.220
Yes.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.240
I'd love to have it at my shop...

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.010
Tokitaka-kun, is that you?

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:07.820
S-Sui?

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.820
I didn't think we'd meet 
at a place like this.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.750
We haven't met since our middle 
school graduation, have we?

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.830
That's right.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.500
So you live in this area now, huh?

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:20.330
Yeah.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.000
I live on my own, working part-time,

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:26.880
and come to these markets 
to sell the wares I make.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.880
I'll be
right back
- Owner

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.880
As a nameless artist?

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:40.350
I see.

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.980
Say, you run a shop, don't you?

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.840
No, I work in an office.

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:50.090
You just said you'd like 
something for your shop.

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:56.280
I want to do it someday, but 
I just can't take the plunge.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.420
Yet, when I saw your work,

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:04.330
I couldn't help but think 
about having it at the shop.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.290
Sensei, I have a question.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.550
We're buying lunch today! Let's run!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.090
I never knew you could be 
indecisive about anything.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:13.550
Was I ever that quick on my feet?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.550
I thought you were a 
no-time-like-the-present type of person.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.210
Is it a financial problem?

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:26.270
That place has always been special to me.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.340
It worries me when I think

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.020
I might make a bad move and destroy 
what my grandfather had created.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.530
I'm afraid to take the first step.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:42.500
It's been a while. I'd like 
to visit the shop again.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.500
I'll bring some of my 
tableware over someday.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:48.500
You'd be up for that?

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:49.810
Sure.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.700
That should do it.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:06.360
Rokuhoudou's still going strong, 
when you look at it like this.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:11.650
Tokitaka-kun.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.900
Hey, boss!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.500
Long time.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:17.760
Eh?

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:24.290
Man, I can't believe you'd 
shut down the shop already.

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:28.050
I tried to tell him about your grandpa...

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.200
Hey, are you here for tea?

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.800
I couldn't find the right moment.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.200
I see.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:38.140
Sui, I'm going to use your counter.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.050
Okay.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:42.240
Sorry about that, kid.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.400
Not at all.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:46.670
My grandfather passed away from 
an illness a few years ago.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:50.310
Really? That's a shame.

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.100
My daughter lives in the area.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.370
I wanted to see the boss while I was here.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.320
I see.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.300
This is my grandkid, Tetsurou.

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.870
Hello...

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:04.570
Hello, Tetsurou-kun.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:08.310
You've gotten so tall, though, kid.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:11.130
You remember me?

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:15.460
Yeah, I remember you 
running around all over.

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:18.800
There was another one just 
like you, wasn't there?

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.370
You two would always be 
smiling, helping the boss.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.040
Hey, Tetsu!

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.560
Don't get in his way.

00:10:29.450 --> 00:10:30.350
It's fine.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.670
Are you opening up shop here or something?

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:35.930
Oh, no.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:37.860
Nothing like that yet.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.360
Oh, really?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:45.120
It's so nice inside and you 
look great in the apron.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:48.060
I thought you were about to start something.

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:56.380
I mean, I guess it's not easy inheriting 
a restaurant in this economy.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:00.290
It's a little sad, though.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.490
It's all empty.

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.890
I always felt at home here.

00:11:09.290 --> 00:11:11.900
And the boss was always smiling.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:15.650
I sure did love this place.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:20.650
But it's over now, huh?

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:24.280
Oh, yeah.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.740
Are there any good places 
to eat around here?

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:30.580
There are no good restaurants 
in this shopping district.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:32.600
Oh, yeah?

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.910
See, I was hoping to have 
something here, you know.

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:38.590
Guess I'll find a convenience 
store or something.

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:41.400
Sorry about that.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.720
Not at all, it's fine.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:46.570
Sorry for getting in your way.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:51.230
Too bad about the boss, but I'm glad 
I got to take a look inside the shop.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.550
Let's go, Tetsu.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:58.250
Thanks, boys.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:03.740
Hey, if it's all right with you, would you 
like to stay for tea and a light meal?

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:11.870
<b>Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori</b>

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.080
Rokuhoudou Yotsuiro Biyori.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:18.760
Tokitaka-kun, is it all right if 
we use the tableware you brought?

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:20.590
Of course.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:23.260
Let's start with this teacup, then.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.660
Hey, by the way, Sui...

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.470
What are you going to do for a light meal?

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.630
I got this.

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:31.980
I'll whip something up in no time.

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.650
Group 3's pepper steak is on fire!

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:37.940
<i>I'll never forget Sui's tales of 
triumph during cooking class.</i>

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:37.940
What the heck are you doing, Kyousui?!

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:41.970
Sui, would you please let me cook?

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:43.800
Really?

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:45.700
I'm good at cooking.

00:12:46.460 --> 00:12:48.460
Thanks, Tokitaka-kun.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:49.450
I owe you.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.840
Feel free to use anything here.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.710
Sorry for imposing, kid.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:03.850
Lucky us, huh, Tetsu?

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:04.380
Yeah.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.410
I'm happy, to be honest, though.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.760
I can't believe I get 
to have tea here again.

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.800
I usually have coffee,

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:16.830
but I'd always have tea when I was here.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.060
Is that so?

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:21.570
Grandpa, look, it's a kaiju!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.480
You're amazing, Tetsu.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:26.420
Look, now it's an airplane.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:28.320
Show me more.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:34.200
<i>I'm making tea for someone who 
loved Grandpa's Rokuhoudou.</i>

00:13:36.510 --> 00:13:39.440
<i>If he doesn't like my tea...</i>

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.800
<i>If I find out that I'm not cut 
out to take over Rokuhoudou...</i>

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.300
<i>But...</i>

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.720
It's over now, huh?

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:51.760
<i>When I heard him say that, I felt like 
shouting that I wouldn't have it.</i>

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.850
<i>I may not be able to make 
it the same way he did,</i>

00:13:56.850 --> 00:14:00.810
<i>but I don't want that man 
to go home feeling empty.</i>

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:04.550
<i>Here you are.</i>

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.400
Sencha and Japanese omurice.

00:14:07.850 --> 00:14:09.660
Well, this is fancy.

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:14.260
I've never seen grated 
daikon on omurice before.

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:17.000
And for you, Tetsurou-kun, milk tea.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.040
Thank you.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:21.040
The tableware is nice and classy, too.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:24.280
All right, Tetsu, let's appreciate the meal.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:25.810
Okay.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:27.300
Time to eat.

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:34.810
The egg's nicely soft-boiled.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.200
And what's this?

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.810
The rice inside is so delicious.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:42.980
We had onions and carrots and small fish,

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.530
so I made small fish butter rice.

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:48.150
The sauce is made from noodle soup base.

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:50.400
You're right.

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:52.150
There's small fish in here.

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.490
You're okay with it, Tetsu?

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.990
Did he not like small fish?

00:14:57.990 --> 00:15:01.670
No, well, he doesn't like fish.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:06.380
He'd never eat even the smallest 
piece of fish at home.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:08.060
But look at him.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:11.240
Your fish rice is so good, mister.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.100
I love it.

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.910
Oh, yeah?

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.070
We'll have to report to Mom about this.

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:20.670
Come on, now. I know it's 
good, but take your time.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.860
So this is the second generation's tea.

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.970
What a pretty sunset.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:03.960
It's not quite like the boss's.

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:07.010
<i>Am I not good enough?</i>

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.080
How should I put it...

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.970
It's not as bitter as his.

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:16.980
It makes me want more.

00:16:19.130 --> 00:16:21.250
Yeah, it goes down easy.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:24.320
So, with that said, more, please.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.050
Get a grip, man.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.010
Oh, sorry.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.230
I thought you might not like it.

00:16:34.230 --> 00:16:36.390
Have some confidence.

00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:42.390
It doesn't taste the same, but you put 
care into your work, just like the boss.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.250
I love it.

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:51.550
For a second, when I thought 
I blew it, my mind went blank.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:58.180
But when I knew he liked it, 
I was so happy, I had the shivers.

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:01.790
It started with your grandpa's Rokuhoudou,

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:06.920
but it was the current Rokuhoudou 
that brought those two smiles.

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.530
Your Rokuhoudou, Sui.

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.620
<i>I think I get it now.</i>

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:17.850
<i>It's because of that smile that 
Grandpa could work every day,</i>

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:21.350
<i>whether it was sweaty or chilly.</i>

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:30.270
"Someday" is never going to come 
if I keep saying "someday."

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.520
Sui, so...

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:40.330
Thank you very much, too, Tokitaka-kun.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:45.720
It's partly thanks to you that 
the two enjoyed their visit.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.640
I've always been making tableware,

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:54.840
but I haven't had much of a 
chance to see people use it.

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:58.610
So it was really new to me.

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.520
The food, the plates...

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:07.350
Seeing my work make people 
happy really is amazing.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.690
Tokitaka-kun...

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:13.360
Hey, if it's all right with you...

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.930
Is there anything I can help with?

00:18:20.920 --> 00:18:22.660
<i>Oh, right.</i>

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.880
<i>I need to let him know, too.</i>

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:30.580
Hey, you're awake.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.580
I'm getting back to cleaning.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:35.710
Right.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:36.590
I'll be right there.

00:18:42.910 --> 00:18:46.320
Sorry, I dozed off.

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:47.450
Sui.

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.020
I've rarely seen you sleep so well.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:52.560
Let's finish cleaning and have some sweets.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:57.380
Tsubaki-kun's making us 
some special desserts.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:18:59.540
I never said that.

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.990
But it's going to be something 
that's not on the menu.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.280
Thank you.

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:06.610
I can't wait for Tsubaki-kun's desserts.

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.990
Sui, can we talk later?

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:10.330
Okay?

00:19:15.600 --> 00:19:17.310
It's all clean.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:19.330
Sui, uh...

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.850
I found this while I was 
cleaning the kitchen.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:29.350
Sorry, I might have broken 
them at some point.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.100
I didn't know we still had these.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:37.260
No, these broke a long time ago.

00:19:37.260 --> 00:19:39.240
I just couldn't bring 
myself to throw them out.

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:44.660
It's been a while since 
we've had you over, Yakyou.

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:46.160
Yeah...

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:49.700
You don't have to go, just because it's 
the school your dad picked out for you.

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:51.760
Knowing you...

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:54.610
I've been thinking, too.

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:58.920
Grandpa's slowly teaching me 
how to make tea right now.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:04.400
I want to learn to make tea 
and coffee like Grandpa does.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:07.630
And someday, I want to run this shop.

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:08.930
And then one day, maybe the two of us can...

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.040
Are you all right?

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.690
That's your teacup.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.000
You can throw it out.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:20.970
I'm not coming back.

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:31.350
Sorry, could you put this back away?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.100
Sure.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.230
Sui, the desserts are ready.

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:36.770
Can you make tea?

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:38.710
I'll be right there.

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.300
Thank you.

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:49.330
<i>I hope you can have tea together again.</i>

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:51.370
Sui.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:52.680
Let's eat here.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:53.980
It looks good.

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.150
Sure, sure.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.810
Hang on.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.390
I'm going to make some tea.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.690
Yoink.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:01.350
Hey!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:06.710
<i>It hasn't been all happy things 
since we opened Rokuhoudou.</i>

00:21:06.710 --> 00:21:07.310
It's good.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:11.430
<i>There's been sad things and 
important things that happened.</i>

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:16.830
<i>It's not as though I'm not worried 
about the future, either.</i>

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:18.640
<i>But still,</i>

00:21:20.020 --> 00:21:23.670
<i>all those smiles have 
kept me going until now.</i>

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.550
<i>If he asked the same question again today...</i>

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:35.390
Kyousui... Do you really
 love this place that much?

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:39.770
<i>I would probably answer the same way.</i>

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:42.840
Yes.

00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:18.590
Omurice has some depth, doesn't it?

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:30.140
<b>Next episode</b>

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:30.140
<b>"Vegetable Power"
 "I Love Ice Cream"</b>

00:23:18.590 --> 00:23:19.380
What do you mean?

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:22.660
Whether it's omusoba or omucurry,

00:23:22.660 --> 00:23:24.610
it can envelop even strong flavors nicely.

00:23:24.610 --> 00:23:27.270
Maybe I'll try putting 
Japanese snacks in omurice.

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:30.140
<b>Come again soon.</b>

00:23:27.270 --> 00:23:28.860
That may be too much.
